<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Gulistan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1804-1813">Russo-Persian War (1804–1813)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Gulistan was signed in October 1813 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1804-1813">Russo-Persian War</a> of 1804–1813. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> recognised Russian possession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> and most of the khanates of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talysh">Talysh</a>, and granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> exclusive naval rights on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. Disputes over its vague borders led to a new war in 1826 and to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turkmenchay">Treaty of Turkmenchay</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-gulistan.jpg" alt="Treaty of Gulistan" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Siamax Original uploader was Kaveh at fa.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gulistan-Treaty.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
